faq:
  - q: What is the minimum order quantity for custom embroidery at Silverscreen Decoration & Fulfillment?
    lead: Silverscreen Decoration & Fulfillment does not require a minimum order quantity for our embroidery services.
    a: Whether you need a single custom sample or a large-scale production run for corporate apparel, our Reno, NV facility is equipped to handle orders of any size. With 50 commercial embroidery machines, we provide scalable, high-quality solutions tailored to your specific business needs.
  - q: Do you charge a digitization fee, and do I own the resulting embroidery file?
    lead: Yes, we charge a fair rate for our in-house digitization services, and you can retain the resulting files.
    a: Our expert digitizers ensure your logo or design is perfectly translated for precise stitching. We can also recommend high-quality external services to help you build and maintain your own permanent design library for future use.
  - q: What types of embroidery thread do you use, and can you match my brand's Pantone colors?
    lead: We use premium Madeira Poly Neon thread and can closely match your brand's specific Pantone colors.
    a: We maintain a massive assortment of in-house thread colors and can custom-order any specific shade Madeira offers. This ensures your corporate uniforms and promotional products reflect your exact brand identity with flawless accuracy.
  - q: Can you execute 3D puff embroidery, and what are the design limitations?
    lead: Yes, we specialize in 3D puff embroidery and have virtually no limitations on executing this dynamic style.
    a: By importing our own high-quality puff materials, we create a bold, raised, and tactile finish that is perfect for hats and outerwear. This advanced capability adds texture and dimension, ensuring your branded apparel truly stands out.
  - q: What is the maximum design size and stitch count you can embroider?
    lead: We can accommodate extremely large designs and unlimited stitch counts utilizing our advanced Tajima commercial embroidery machines.
    a: Equipped with oversized magnetic hoops, our cutting-edge machinery is specifically designed to handle massive, intricate artwork on various garments. This allows us to deliver precision and uncompromising quality on even the most demanding oversized projects. If we can hoop it we can embroider it.
  - q: Is Silverscreen Decoration & Fulfillment able to embroider complex items like hats, bags, and heavy outerwear?
    lead: Yes, we possess the specialized expertise and equipment required to embroider complex items and high-value garments.
    a: From delicate fabrics to heavy-duty workwear, bags, and structured hats, our experienced team excels at hard-to-perform applications. We ensure a flawless, professional finish across a diverse range of challenging apparel types.
  - q: What backing material do you use for embroidery, and will it irritate the skin?
    lead: We offer multiple high-quality backing options designed to provide structural stability to the design without irritating the skin.
    a: Our team selects the appropriate backing based on the garment's fabric type and intended use. This meticulous attention to detail ensures superior comfort, wearability, and durability for all corporate wear, retail, and team apparel.
  - q: What are your standard turnaround times for embroidery, and do you accept rush orders?
    lead: Our standard turnaround time for embroidery projects is 5 to 7 days, and we readily accommodate firm deadlines or rush orders.
    a: Operating 50 commercial embroidery machines across two full shifts gives us unparalleled efficiency and capacity. If you have an urgent request, our scalable operations guarantee we can meet your tightest deadlines without compromising on our unwavering quality.
  - q: Do you offer a physical pre-production sample for approval before running the full order?
    lead: Yes, we provide physical pre-production sew-out samples to ensure your complete satisfaction before full production begins.
    a: We prefer working with high-quality sample art provided by the client to achieve the most accurate representation of the final product. This step ensures that every stitch aligns perfectly with your vision and brand standards.
